quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  11,20,"They shall never be able to escape on the earth, nor shall they have helpers besides Allah. The punishment will be multiplied for them, for they could neither listen nor did they use to see."
  11,21,"They are the ones who have lost their souls, and what they used to fabricate has deserted them."
  11,22,"There is no doubt that in the Hereafter, they shall be the greatest losers."
  11,23,"Indeed, those who believe, perform righteous deeds and are humble before their Lord—they shall be the residents of Paradise (and) they shall remain in it forever."
  11,24,"The example of two groups is like that of one blind and deaf, and the other seeing and hearing—can they be equal in comparison? Will you not then be mindful of advice?"
  11,25,"Indeed, We sent Nuh (Noah) to his people, (declaring:) ‘I am a clear warner to you,"
  11,26,"that you shall worship none but Allah. Indeed, I fear for you the punishment of a painful day.’"
  11,27,"But the influential disbelievers among his people said: ‘We do not consider you but a human being like us. And we do not see anyone following you except those who are the most ignoble among us, as is clear to find. And we do not see you having any merit over us. Instead, we think that you are liars.’"
  11,28,"He said: ‘O my people! Tell me: If I stand upon a clear proof from my Lord, and He has granted me mercy from Himself, and it has been made invisible to you, shall we force it upon you while you are unwilling to accept it?"
